.TH zwmem "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zwmem \- dock widget: free memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
started by \fBzdock\fR (catalog line \fB@Memory:/usr/hr/bin/zwmem\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zwmem -- dock widget: free memory
Started by zdock from an @ line of /usr/hr/etc/dock; not run by hand.
Shows free user memory (Kb) in a cell of the dock bar.
.HE
.B zwmem
is a widget of the
.B zdock
bar: a small resident program the dock starts from an
.B @
line of its catalog, showing the machine's free user memory in
kilobytes in an icon-sized cell at the right end of the bar.
The figure is
.BR mem 's
(and
.BR zmon 's):
the kernel's in-core segment queue, walked through a
.B /dev/kmem
snapshot, subtracted from the user-memory span.
It resamples every three seconds.
.PP
It draws inside the dock's own window under the dock's clipping, owns
no window of its own, and takes no input itself; a left click on the
cell is the dock's, and the shipped catalog wires it to
.B zmon
(switch to it when it runs, launch it when it does not), so the
Monitor icon need not sit on the bar.
It exits by itself when the dock goes away.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 8n 30n
	/coherent	kernel namelist
	/dev/kmem	kernel memory
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B zdock ,
.B zview ,
.B zmon ,
.B mem
.SH NOTES
Not meant to be run from a shell: it needs the cell contract
.RB ( \-W )
that only
.B zdock
supplies, and exits at once without it.
With no readable
.B /dev/kmem
or a stripped kernel the cell shows
.B \-\-
and keeps ticking.
For the full memory breakdown and process list, see
.BR zmon .
